<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Assignment 8.3 — Magazine Layout Using Grid Areas</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Main Grid Container -->
    <div class="magazine-grid">
        
        <!-- Header Section -->
        <header class="mag-header">
            <h1>The Daily Chronicle</h1>
            <p class="date-stamp">Sunday, October 25, 2026</p>
        </header>

        <!-- Navigation Section -->
        <nav class="mag-nav">
            <ul>
                <li><a href="#" class="active">World</a></li>
                <li><a href="#">Technology</a></li>
                <li><a href="#">Design</a></li>
                <li><a href="#">Culture</a></li>
                <li><a href="#">Business</a></li>
            </ul>
        </nav>

        <!-- Main Article Section -->
        <main class="mag-main">
            <article class="hero-story">
                <span class="category-tag">Featured Story</span>
                <h2>The Architecture of Modern Grid Systems</h2>
                <p class="lead-text">
                    How named template fields are changing the layout paradigms of digital editorial design platforms across the open web.
                </p>
                <div class="story-body">
                    <p>For decades, digital layouts struggled to mirror the intricate structural flexibility of print media. Designers fought with floats, inline-blocks, and early flex hacks to align columns cleanly without breaking flow containers.</p>
                    <p>With the widespread adoption of <code>grid-template-areas</code>, editorial design has experienced a modern renaissance. Developers can explicitly declare page maps directly inside parent selectors, defining visual hierarchies that adapt seamlessly to responsive changes.</p>
                </div>
            </article>
        </main>

        <!-- Sidebar Section -->
        <aside class="mag-sidebar">
            <div class="sidebar-block">
                <h3>Trending News</h3>
                <ul class="trending-list">
                    <li>
                        <span class="trend-num">01</span>
                        <a href="#">Quantum computing layers pass network latency tests.</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="trend-num">02</span>
                        <a href="#">Designing for accessibility: A checklist for engineering teams.</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="trend-num">03</span>
                        <a href="#">CSS custom properties evolve to support dynamic structural state triggers.</a>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </aside>

        <!-- Footer Section -->
        <footer class="mag-footer">
            <p>&copy; 2026 The Daily Chronicle Editorial Team. Crafted using explicit CSS named grid areas.</p>
        </footer>

    </div>

</body>
</html>











/* ==========================================
   BASE EDITORIAL RESET
   ========================================== */
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

body {
    font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; /* Classic editorial typography */
    background-color: #fcfbf7; /* Warm soft newsprint color */
    color: #1a1a1a;
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding: 20px;
}

/* ==========================================
   GRID CONTAINER & AREA DECLARATIONS
   ========================================== */
.magazine-grid {
    display: grid;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    gap: 24px;

    /* Step 5: Allocates three columns. The main article spans 2 columns (1fr + 1fr),
       giving it double the structural space of the 1fr sidebar. */
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
    
    /* Step 3: Global template matrix map specifying spatial structural flow lines */
    grid-template-areas: 
        "head head head"
        "navigation navigation navigation"
        "main main side"
        "foot foot foot";
}

/* ==========================================
   ASSIGNING NAMED GRID AREAS (Step 4)
   ========================================== */
.mag-header {
    grid-area: head;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 30px 0;
    border-bottom: 4px double #1a1a1a;
}

.mag-nav {
    grid-area: navigation;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a;
    padding: 10px 0;
}

.mag-main {
    grid-area: main;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #e8e6df;
    padding: 30px;
}

.mag-sidebar {
    grid-area: side;
    background-color: #f7f5ee;
    border-left: 1px solid #dcdad0;
    padding: 24px;
}

.mag-footer {
    grid-area: foot;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 24px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #1a1a1a;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #666666;
}

/* ==========================================
   INTERNAL COMPONENT STYLING
   ========================================== */

/* --- Header Elements --- */
.mag-header h1 {
    font-size: 3.5rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -1px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
}
.date-stamp {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    color: #555555;
}

/* --- Navigation Links --- */
.mag-nav ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 40px;
}
.mag-nav a {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: #333333;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
}
.mag-nav a:hover, .mag-nav a.active {
    color: #c2410c;
}

/* --- Main Story Layout --- */
.category-tag {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    color: #c2410c;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
}
.hero-story h2 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    margin: 8px 0 16px 0;
    line-height: 1.2;
}
.lead-text {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #333333;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-style: italic;
}
.story-body p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    text-align: justify;
}

/* --- Sidebar Content --- */
.sidebar-block h3 {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #1a1a1a;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
}
.trending-list {
    list-style: none;
}
.trending-list li {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: flex-start;
}
.trend-num {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #c2410c;
    line-height: 1;
}
.trending-list a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: bold;
}
.trending-list a:hover {
    color: #c2410c;
}

/* ==========================================
   RESPONSIVE DESIGN SYSTEM MEDIA QUERY
   ========================================== */
@media (max-width: 868px) {
    /* Step 6: Transforms structural layouts dynamically into 
       a single-column grid context for phone displays. */
    .magazine-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        grid-template-areas: 
            "head"
            "navigation"
            "main"
            "side"
            "foot";
    }
    
    .mag-sidebar {
        border-left: none;
        border-top: 1px solid #dcdad0;
    }
    
    .mag-nav ul {
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 20px;
    }
}
